  "summary": "CLI tooling: static patterns in test fixtures and agent templates, no traced installer harm",
  "details": "a static rule hits are concentrated in test files and agent/template scripts shipped as developer tooling. The curl/wget references in dist/services/codex-pre-tool-hook-template.test.js and codex-pre-tool-policy-template.js are policy/test fixtures (example URLs like releases.hashicorp.com, example.com, and clearly-labeled evil.test strings used as negative test cases for a pre-tool policy template). Buffer.from(..., 'base64') usage in global-codex-config.js and the related test, plus the GitHub-deploy skill script, is routine base64 encoding/decoding of config and release artifacts, not fetch-and-eval. The api-mcp-runtime.mjs ping/GET/POST tokens correspond to an HTTP client template, not an install-time exfiltration path. No lifecycle script fetches and executes remote content, no installer-side credential paths (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, browser stores) are read and shipped off-host, and no hardcoded attacker destination is bound to a network sink.",
